d><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math><br /><br />For differentiability at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> . This with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> gives the values <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />then <math xmlns=\"htt